'{"corrected_text":"By the Judge—The wounds were not sufficient\\nto produce the fatal syncope.\\nExamination continued—The syncope came on\\nfrom natural causes, and the wounds did not, I\\nbelieve, contribute to cause death. Any hard sub¬\\stance would produce the bruises on the arms.\\nThe bruises might have been got by falling over\\na heap of stones. I cannot believe that\\nhemorrhage was the cause of death. Death, I\\nthink, was the result of a combination of disease\\nof the brain, disease of the heart, and intemper¬\\ate habits.","has_modifications":true}'
